// A type error in the SECOND file of a multi-file package must report THAT
// file's real path and THAT file's own line:column.
//
// This is why concat_package_sources had to be deleted rather than taught to
// handle several package clauses. Concatenation reported the IMPORT PATH as the
// filename and a concat-relative line number, so the same error surfaced as
// "./multifile:21:8" — a line that exists in no file, attributed to a name that
// is not a file. PRs #221-#223 spent three PRs making diagnostics report true
// positions; a concatenating multi-file path would have silently undone that
// for every package the moment it shipped.
//
// The sidecar asserts the file name AND the line:column together, so a
// regression in either one fails this fixture.
package main

import "./multifilebad"

func main() {
	_ = multifilebad.Good()
}
